From 14c4f6e6dbd5b55c8c865ab8902c562ab0960260 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 18:59:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02650/11362] [outer-loop] Eval Qwopus3.6-27B-Coder-MTP vs
 gemma-12B on Layer B: MTP works (80% accept, 1.5x) but 27B still slower than
 12B on the iGPU; accuracy comparable

Operator request: try the OSS SOTA coder Jackrong/Qwopus3.6-27B-Coder-MTP-GGUF with MTP for faster + more
accurate Layer-B induction. Tested on the offline iGPU (port 8921, NOT the 3090s).

Setup: llama.cpp 9606 already has native --spec-type draft-mtp (no rebuild). Self-MTP loads the -MTP-
GGUF as both target+draft (~32GB shared RAM). Q4_K_M, Qwen3.6-27B coder, SWE-bench 67%.

Results (same scaffolded prompt as the gemma sweep):
- ka59: Tier2 GROUNDED both no-MTP (2.74 t/s) and MTP (3.40 t/s, 1.24x).
- tn36: Tier2 GROUNDED no-MTP (1.54 t/s); MTP 2.98 t/s (1.93x) but Tier0 -- that flip is temp-0.2
  sampling variance, NOT MTP loss (spec-decoding is lossless only at greedy/temp0; ka59 grounded both).
- MTP draft acceptance 0.806 (high) -> ~1.5x real speedup, matches the card's 1.66x.

Honest bottom line: (1) accuracy COMPARABLE, no advantage on this task -- Qwopus grounds the same
count-class games gemma already grounds and is more concise; it does NOT unlock cd82/wa30 (those fail
on DIGEST SHAPE -- ~10k/6.3k-tok flat-array prompts for large-2D editable regions -- not model strength).
For Config Layer B the model is not the bottleneck, the digest is. (2) Speed: even with MTP the 27B is
SLOWER than the 12B on the iGPU (~3 vs ~4.2 t/s); MTP's 1.5x does not overcome the 2.25x param gap. The
card's ~100 t/s is fast-GPU territory (3090 off-limits here). Recommendation: keep gemma-12B default for
Layer B; reach for Qwopus+MTP for harder coding where 27B quality matters, ideally on a fast GPU. MTP
itself is a clean free speedup worth using whenever this model runs. Adversarial-verify clean.

